      "id": "grammar-insistir-en-que-claim",
      "kind": "grammar",
      "promptEs": "insistir en que + afirmación",
      "questionEn": "How do you say that someone keeps firmly claiming that a statement is true?",
      "answerEn": "Use a form of insistir, then en que, then state the claim.",
      "noteEn": "Insistir changes for the person and time, but en is required before the claim. Que introduces the statement being asserted. This card covers insisting that something is true; pressing another person to perform an action can use a different verb form after que.",
      "example": {
        "es": "Leo insiste en que el informe es correcto.",
        "en": "Leo insists that the report is correct."
      },
      "tags": [
        "grammar",
